    {
        "content": "<p>Hello! For the last couple of days I’ve been experimenting with an AI-generated candidate proof and Lean formalization of the k = 5 case of Dean’s conjecture. As far as I can tell, this is the remaining open case, so if the argument holds up, it would complete the conjecture.</p>\n<p>Repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/pkchv/dean-conjecture\">https://github.com/pkchv/dean-conjecture</a></p>\n<p>Any feedback on this would be very welcome.</p>",
        "id": 613550507,
        "sender_full_name": "Kamil Sieniawski",
        "timestamp": 1785376053
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Cool! The <a href=\"https://github.com/pkchv/dean-conjecture/blob/eee0a3f0a1fdc42f11d93bec1a64957f4e5511b4/DeanK5Challenge.lean\">challenge</a> file looks alright, but is stated a bit awkwardly. Could you use this instead?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dean_conjecture_k5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Adj</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">minDegree</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsCycle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∣</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I think using <code>minDegree</code> explicitly makes more sense.</p>",
